From 01a75a449f318984bdfdd33008e840e12c2e1f88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:41:53 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Arena: a series you can leave, give up, clear or lose

A monster series is now a Gauntlet of twelve rounds that survives a break.
After a win the attendant reports the round ("Round n of 12 won! Step into the
circle when you are ready."), the series keeps running, and the player is placed
outside the circle, facing it, instead of inside it (which started the next
fight at once); the gate resumes it. Talking to the attendant while a series
runs asks "Do you want to give up?" Yes ends it (not a loss; the best streak is
kept), No says "Good luck!". Clearing round 12 is a win and ends the series
with its own line. A loss ends it as before and now restores the party to full
HP and PP. The stock record write into a file is skipped (no saving messages,
no "current file" after New Game); the tallies are saved with the game.

scene/arena_series.c is a part of battle_arena.c (it uses that file's statics).
The round count is in module/arena.h and asserted against the message text.
Three messages are added. Switch: ARENA_TRAINING.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
